# Containers and Deployment

- Use minimal supported base images pinned by digest and deterministic locked installs.
- Never publish production `latest` tags. Build once and promote the same immutable artifact.
- Run non-root with only required capabilities; prefer read-only filesystems and explicit writable mounts.
- Keep secrets out of images and plaintext configuration. Use managed runtime secret references.
- Define resource limits, graceful shutdown, restart behavior, persistent storage, and backup ownership.
- Liveness checks process state; readiness checks mandatory dependencies. Auth redirects are not backend health.
- CI must verify policy, formatting, types, tests, security, dependencies, build, SBOM, image, provenance, and docs as applicable.
- Production needs review, environment approval, recovery evidence, post-deploy validation, and rollback.
- Do not trust a persistent self-hosted runner for provenance until its isolation and secret handling are proven.
